enue guidance.\nDelta Air Lines (NYSE:DAL) forecast its fourth-quarter unit revenue to rise by 3%, compared to 3% to 5% in prior guidance, with earnings per share of $1.25 to $1.30.\n“The pace of improvement in late December was more modest than anticipated,” Delta said in its updated guidance.\nThe news follows downbeat revenue forecasts from Apple (NASDAQ:AAPL), which cited a decline in Chinese iPhone sales. The lower forecasts prompted worries that the U.S.-China trade tensions are contributing to a global slowdown.\nDelta was down 8.5%, while American Airlines Group (NASDAQ:AAL) slumped 7.8%, United Continental (NASDAQ:UAL) fell 6% and Southwest Airlines (NYSE:LUV) slipped 3.2%. The declines were in line with broader markets , with the Dow down more than 500 points.\nRelated Articles\nAB Inbev's Zimbabwe unit scraps hard currency payment plan after govt opposition\nForeigners pull most cash from Asian equities in at least 7 years in 2018\nChina stocks higher at close of trade; Shanghai Composite up 2.05%", "external_links": ["https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/stocks--wall-street-slumps-as-lowered-apple-guidance-spooks-investors-1736275?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=yahoo_finance&quot;", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/excredit-suisse-bankers-arrested-on-us-charges-over-mozambique-loans-1736911?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=yahoo_finance&quot;", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/stocks--wall-street-slumps-as-lowered-apple-guidance-spooks-investors-1736275?utm_source=yahoo&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=yahoo_finance", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/excredit-suisse-bankers-arrested-on-us-charges-over-mozambique-loans-1736911?utm_source=yahoo&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=yahoo_finance", "https://www.investing.com/news/technology-news/apple-shares-slide-after-iphone-maker-issues-rare-revenue-warning-1736150?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium